# smbclient

`smbclient` is a command-line client for interacting with SMB/CIFS servers and Windows file shares.

It can be used to enumerate shares, access files, upload/download data, and interact with SMB services.

Personal notes and reference for SMB enumeration and testing.

---

# Basic Syntax

```bash
smbclient //<IP>/<SHARE> [options]
```

---

# List Shares

```text
-L //<IP>
```

Lists available SMB shares.

Useful for initial SMB enumeration.

---

# Connect to a Share

```text
smbclient //<IP>/<SHARE>
```

Connects to a specific SMB share.

Anonymous access can sometimes be tested with:

```text
-N
```

---

# Authentication

### Username

```text
-U <USERNAME>
```

### Password

```text
-p <PASSWORD>
```

### Anonymous

```text
-N
```

Avoid putting passwords directly in command history when possible.

---

# Workgroup / Domain

```text
-W <WORKGROUP>
```

Specify the workgroup or Windows domain.

---

# SMB Protocol Version

```text
-m <PROTOCOL>
```

Can be used to specify the SMB protocol version.

Common protocols include:

```text
SMB2
SMB3
NT1
```

---

# Common Options

| Option | Description |
|---|---|
| `-L` | List available shares |
| `-U` | Specify username |
| `-N` | No password prompt |
| `-p` | Specify password |
| `-W` | Specify workgroup/domain |
| `-m` | Specify maximum SMB protocol |
| `-I` | Specify destination IP |
| `-c` | Execute commands |
| `-d` | Debug level |
| `-s` | Specify configuration file |
| `-g` | Machine-readable output |
| `-A` | Authentication file |

