# Useful Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `smbclient -L //<IP>` | List shares |
| `smbclient -L //<IP> -N` | List shares anonymously |
| `smbclient //<IP>/<SHARE>` | Connect to a share |
| `smbclient //<IP>/<SHARE> -N` | Anonymous connection |
| `smbclient //<IP>/<SHARE> -U <USER>` | Authenticated connection |
| `get <FILE>` | Download file |
| `put <FILE>` | Upload file |
| `ls` | List files |
| `cd <DIR>` | Change directory |
| `pwd` | Show current directory |
| `-c "<COMMAND>"` | Execute command |

---

# Notes

- SMB stands for **Server Message Block**.
- CIFS is an older implementation/dialect of SMB.
- Port `445` is the main SMB port encountered in modern environments.
- `-L` is useful for initial share enumeration.
- `-N` can test anonymous access.
- Access to a share does not necessarily mean read/write access.
- Always check what permissions are available.
- SMB shares can contain sensitive configuration files, backups, credentials, or other useful information.
- Only access SMB services you are authorized to test.

